 | M14 player model     | written without a toolchain: not compiled, not run (+3 tests in `player.rs`, +1 in `touch_ui.rs`) | `render/player.rs`: b1.7.3 `ModelBiped` + `mob/char.png` with walk / sneak / riding / arm-swing animation, in the third-person view (new view button) and as the inventory preview. No armor, ears, cloak or hurt flash. See ROADMAP changelog. |
 | Debug screen (Info) | type-checked for aarch64-linux-android (`cargo check --lib --tests`), not run (+2 tests in `render/debug.rs`, 2 extended in `options.rs`) | `render/debug.rs`: two translucent panels in the GUI scale for screenshots (left: position, chunk, facing, biome, light, time, aimed block; right: FPS, frame time, screen and scene size with the scene scale, Dynamic Res, MSAA, Post, renderer, graphics and smooth lighting, Performance, render distance, chunks, LoD). Pause menu button `Info: on/off` (`debugScreen` in `options.txt`); while on it replaces the FPS counter and the LoD debug title. See the rendering changelog. |
+| Visual polish (Look) | type-checked on a Linux host (`cargo check --lib --tests`, a stand-in `android-activity`), tests of the touched modules pass there, the WGSL validates with naga and every assembled GLSL with glslang; not run on a device (+8 tests in `render/look.rs`, +1 each in `options.rs` and `atmos.rs`, the sky fan test extended) | `render/look.rs` + the final pass and chunk shaders of BOTH renderers: one `Vibrance` dial (Video Settings, default 30%, 0 = off) scales a grade in the final pass (vibrance, not saturation; a gentle S-curve; warm highlights / cool shadows). `Effects...` (Video Settings) has five switches: Warm Light (golden low sun, bluer shade, faces sink a little deeper), Water Look (depth gradient + sun glint), Glow (soft additive halos on lava, torches, glowstone and the sun only), Motion (off / low / on: leaf sway, motes near flowers and water, light rays at a low sun) and Haze (aerial perspective). Capped: 36 halos, 10 / 24 motes, 80 sprites a frame. `look_*` in `options.txt`. See the rendering changelog. |
 | Audio (M9)           | written without a toolchain: not compiled, not run (+3 tests in `audio/`) | `audio/`: `SoundManager` / `SoundPool`. All 194 effects (80 `SoundPool` keys: `step.*`, `mob.*`, `random.*`, `note.*`, `ambient.*`, `liquid.*`, `fire.*`, `portal.*`, `tile.piston.*`, `damage.*`), 12 music tracks and records 13 / cat are embedded from the b1.7.3 asset index (`tools/gen_sounds.py` -> `assets/sound/`, `audio/table.rs`). Software mixer (pitch by resampling, linear distance gain, pan), lewton decoder, AAudio output via `ndk`; music on a stream thread, one random track 10-20 min apart. Wired: Music / Sound options, footsteps, block break sound (`Block.stepSound`, table read from `Block.java`), note blocks, jukebox records. Not wired yet: every other `playSoundEffect` call of the Java (mobs, hurt, doors, buttons, fire, water, explosions, rain, thunder, cave ambience, pistons, portal). The 12 `streaming/*.mus` files are not b1.7.3 and are left out. |
 | Sprint (Retro Sprint port) | written without a toolchain: not compiled, not run (+10 tests: 8 in `world/sprint.rs`, 1 in `mobs.rs`, 1 in `gamepad.rs`) | `world/sprint.rs`: periut's Retro Sprint (b1.7.3 mixins), read from its sources. Double tap forward (touch d-pad arrow, a corner, or the stick pushed up): a tap of at most 4 ticks, then a second press within 7 ticks of its release; a longer press is a walk and never sprints or hold L3 on the pad; sprinting adds 0.035 blocks/tick along the facing (x1.35 of the walk), a jump adds 0.2 blocks/tick, the field of view x1.15 (eased), a hit shoves the target 1.2 blocks/tick and ends the sprint, specks of the block below fly while it runs. Ends on releasing forward / sneaking, a wall, water, riding, sleeping or after 30 s. See the gameplay changelog. |
 | Stamina (Stamina port) | written without a full toolchain: type-checked and `stamina::tests::*` (5) + `vitals::tests::damage_like_java` run in a Linux scratch crate; the HUD and `lib.rs` wiring not run on a device | `world/stamina.rs`: insane96mcp's Stamina (NeoForge 26.1.2), read from its sources, its default numbers. 200 stamina (10 per health point, armor -2.5% a point); a sprint costs 1 a tick (x0.8 out of combat, 15 s after a hit dealt or taken), a jump 10; empty = locked: no sprinting until it regenerates (2 a tick, x0.6 while locked) to 40%; at 20% health the bar is emptied and locked; locked walks x0.9, sprinting under 40 / 20% x0.85 more. HUD: grey half-heart overlay on the hearts it no longer covers (darker while locked), `Stamina` row in the debug screen. Not ported: Vigour / Curse of Weariness, the Vigour effect, swimming, mining cost, hunger spend, the command, the sync, the config. See the gameplay changelog. |
